<p>
  The ToolSetAgent constructs task-specific tool subgraphs via random walks on the full 80,000-tool graph, producing dense dependency structures that average 30+ tools per VitaBench-style task. The UserProfileAgent goes beyond simple personas to model communication style (verbose vs terse), willingness (cooperative vs reluctant), and disclosure patterns (upfront vs need-to-ask). These axes together produce training tasks that genuinely require multi-turn clarification and complex tool orchestration.
</p>
<p>
  The result is strong performance on agentic benchmarks: 70.80 on &#964;&#178;-Bench retail (vs 64.90 for DeepSeek-V3.1 and 64.80 for Kimi-K2) and 24.30 on VitaBench (vs 20.30 and 18.20 respectively).
</p>
</section>

